body:
@normanmaurer #6953 this is OK. Thanks! But what about this:
> a setCharSequence - the only set method which can increase capacity...

IMHO, this is not fine.. For example:
```java
        ByteBuf buf = Unpooled.directBuffer(1);
        buf.setCharSequence(0, "AB", CharsetUtil.US_ASCII); // no exception. capacity == 2

        buf.resetWriterIndex().capacity(1);
        buf.setBytes(0, new byte[]{1, 2}); // IndexOutOfBoundsException
```
I think only `write` methods should increase capacity.
